Subject: [PATCH] wave: measure data IRQ delays from valid monotonic events

The shared tasklet visits empty rings before their first IRQ. Subtracting
an uninitialized realtime timestamp records Unix-epoch nanoseconds as a
permanent maximum; MSI also never populated the old timestamp fields.

Stamp both IRQ paths with monotonic time, sample only nonempty work owned
by that interrupt domain, and retain the same timestamp through processing.
Use native atomic64 values for coherent hardirq/tasklet/control snapshots
on 32-bit hosts. Packet budgets, scheduling and firmware ABI are unchanged.

--- a/wireless/driver/shared/hw_mmb.c
+++ b/wireless/driver/shared/hw_mmb.c
@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@
 
 #include "linux/netdevice.h"
 #include <linux/ktime.h>
+#include <linux/atomic.h>
 #ifdef MTCFG_SET_PM_QOS
 #include "linux/pm_qos.h"
 #endif
